<Base title="Privacy" description="How Polaris Group handles the personal data you send through this site." path="/privacy/">
  <header class="article-head wrap"><h1>Privacy</h1></header>
  <div class="article-body">
    <p>This notice explains what happens to personal data sent through polarisglobal.io.</p>
    <h2>Who is responsible</h2>
    <p>Polaris Group, founded by Marc Taverner, London. <span class="confirm">Confirm legal entity and address</span> Contact: <a href="mailto:marc@bluespheresolutions.co.uk">marc@bluespheresolutions.co.uk</a>.</p>
    <h2>What we collect</h2>
    <p>When you use the contact form we receive your name, email address, organisation if you give it, and your message. The site does not use advertising or tracking cookies.</p>
    <h2>Why and on what basis</h2>
    <p>We use your details only to read and reply to your message and to keep a record of the conversation. The lawful basis is our legitimate interest in responding to enquiries you choose to send.</p>
    <h2>Who processes it</h2>
    <p>Form submissions are received and stored by Netlify, which hosts this site, and forwarded to our email. We do not sell or share your details with anyone else.</p>
    <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
    <p>We keep enquiries for up to two years after our last contact with you, then delete them. <span class="confirm">Confirm retention period</span></p>
    <h2>Your rights</h2>
    <p>You can ask to see, correct or delete the personal data we hold about you, or object to how we use it, by emailing the address above. You can also complain to the Information Commissioner's Office at <a href="https://ico.org.uk/">ico.org.uk</a>.</p>
  </div>
</Base>
